    "body": "### Problem\n\nA headless Nvim RPC server can crash if accepting an incoming `--server` connection fails inside `socket_watcher_accept()`.\n\n`channel_from_connection()` currently ignores the return value from `socket_watcher_accept()` and continues initializing the channel:\n\n```c\nChannel *channel = channel_alloc(kChannelStreamSocket);\nsocket_watcher_accept(watcher, &channel->stream.socket);\nchannel->stream.socket.s.internal_close_cb = close_cb;\nchannel->stream.socket.s.internal_data = channel;\nwstream_init(&channel->stream.socket.s, 0);\nrstream_init(&channel->stream.socket);\nrpc_start(channel);\n```\n\nIf `socket_watcher_accept()` returns an error, it closes the client handle and returns before calling `stream_init()`. The caller still starts RPC on the partially initialized channel. In the observed crash this later reaches:\n\n```text\nSIGSEGV\nfread_idle_cb\nuv__run_idle\nuv_run\nloop_poll_events\ninbuf_poll\ninput_get\nstate_enter\nmain\n```\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nBuild Nvim from source, then create a small preload library that makes one `setsockopt()` call return `EPROTONOSUPPORT`:\n\n```sh\ncat > /tmp/fail_setsockopt.c <<'EOF'\n#include <dlfcn.h>\n#include <errno.h>\n#include <stdatomic.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <sys/socket.h>\n\nstatic int (*real_setsockopt_fn)(int, int, int, const void *, socklen_t);\nstatic atomic_int calls;\nstatic int fail_at = 1;\n\n__attribute__((constructor))\nstatic void init(void)\n{\n  const char *env = getenv(\"FAIL_SETSOCKOPT_AT\");\n  if (env != NULL && *env != '\\0') {\n    fail_at = atoi(env);\n  }\n}\n\nint setsockopt(int fd, int level, int optname, const void *optval, socklen_t optlen)\n{\n  if (real_setsockopt_fn == NULL) {\n    real_setsockopt_fn = dlsym(RTLD_NEXT, \"setsockopt\");\n  }\n\n  int n = atomic_fetch_add(&calls, 1) + 1;\n  if (n == fail_at) {\n    errno = EPROTONOSUPPORT;\n    return -1;\n  }\n\n  return real_setsockopt_fn(fd, level, optname, optval, optlen);\n}\nEOF\n\ncc -dynamiclib -o /tmp/fail_setsockopt.dylib /tmp/fail_setsockopt.c\n```\n\nStart a headless Nvim RPC server:\n\n```sh\nrm -f /tmp/nvim-accept.sock\n\nFAIL_SETSOCKOPT_AT=1 \\\nDYLD_INSERT_LIBRARIES=/tmp/fail_setsockopt.dylib \\\nDYLD_FORCE_FLAT_NAMESPACE=1 \\\nbuild/bin/nvim --clean -u NONE -n --headless --listen /tmp/nvim-accept.sock &\nserver=$!\n\nsleep 1\n```\n\nConnect from a clean client process:\n\n```sh\nbuild/bin/nvim --clean -u NONE -n --headless \\\n  --server /tmp/nvim-accept.sock \\\n  --remote-expr '1'\n\nwait \"$server\"\n```\n\nObserved result: the client reports that the channel was closed by the peer, and the Nvim server exits with `SIGSEGV`.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe failed accept should reject only that connection. The Nvim server should remain alive and continue accepting later RPC clients.\n\n### Suggested fix\n\nCheck the return value from `socket_watcher_accept()` before initializing the channel:\n\n```diff\ndiff --git a/src/nvim/channel.c b/src/nvim/channel.c\n--- a/src/nvim/channel.c\n+++ b/src/nvim/channel.c\n@@\n void channel_from_connection(SocketWatcher *watcher)\n {\n   Channel *channel = channel_alloc(kChannelStreamSocket);\n-  socket_watcher_accept(watcher, &channel->stream.socket);\n+  int result = socket_watcher_accept(watcher, &channel->stream.socket);\n+  if (result != 0) {\n+    ELOG(\"Failed to accept connection: %s\", uv_strerror(result));\n+    channel_destroy_early(channel);\n+    return;\n+  }\n   channel->stream.socket.s.internal_close_cb = close_cb;\n   channel->stream.socket.s.internal_data = channel;\n   wstream_init(&channel->stream.socket.s, 0);\n```\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-1249+g3a39646693\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nN/A. This uses Nvim’s `--listen` / `--server` RPC channel path.\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nmacOS 26.6.1 arm64\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nN/A, reproduced with `--headless`.\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nN/A, reproduced with `--headless`.\n\n### Installation\n\nBuilt from source from the Neovim GitHub repository.",
